- Differences, none of which matters:
  - one arm per process instead of all arms in one process, so the reference is recomputed in each process (it is deterministic, and the error fields are identical across processes);
  - solve counts are 1 and 1+N instead of 5/1 (whole) and 3/5 (stage);
  - the probe drops spectral_bounds and the rho_bar/explicit_step_bound fields (a pure function);
  - it adds success, state_fnv1a, per-solve times and full-precision {:e} output;
  - it wraps results in black_box;
  - it panics on an unknown arm, where the test falls through to verified;
  - the gmres-identity process also builds the unused longitude preconditioner (outside the timed region, and it cancels in C(1+N)-C(1));
  - the release profile is the same, but `cargo test --release` would build with panic=unwind while the probe uses abort;
  - all 93 dependency versions and checksums in the probe lockfile match the workspace Cargo.lock.
- One difference helps: the PLAN's command `cargo test -- --ignored` would run the two ignored diagnostics concurrently under libtest's default thread pool, and perf would count every arm together. The probe avoids both.
